# New UI must localize all current languages (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-21), verbatim intent:

> **Hard Rule: when implementing new code and UI interfaces, they must all
> support full localization of all current languages. We do not want any
> leakage. The exception is training guides and manuals for the moment
> which are prepared for localization but don't have localized text yet.**

Same-day clarification:

> **All agents support all language localization. Installers are
> configured only for English and German for the moment.**

“All agents” means **product** agents (AIC Agent, Workstation Assurance,
Jump / recording / DB agents, elevate helpers, and their shipping GUI/CLI
chrome) — **not** Cursor AI agents.

## The rule

> **New code and operator UI ship with catalogs for every currently shipped
> content language in the same change set. English-only chrome is leakage.
> Product agents follow that bar. Installer wizard / setup languages are
> English and German only for now (Partial — not Tier 1 complete). Training
> guides and operator manuals are prepared (US English source +
> localization-work queue) without localized body text yet. Product chrome
> around those manuals still localizes.**

## Three-way split (do not collapse)

| Surface | Languages now | Status word |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Product agents, admin SPA, configurators, elevate helpers, API chrome** | Every **currently shipped** content language, same change set | Full current-language coverage required. Do not invent a shorter list. |
| **Installers** (MSI / WiX / setup wizard / installer language picker / installer-configured UI) | **`en` and `de` only** for this phase | **Partial.** Do **not** claim Tier 1 installer complete. Do not add `fr` / `es` / `zh-*` / `en-GB` wizard catalogs in this phase. |
| **Training guides and operator manuals** (repo SOPs under `docs/ops/`, future in-product Documentation chapters, MSP/C3PAO demo training guide) | US English source + queue row; **no** localized body text required yet | Prepared, not localized. Do **not** claim the manual is localized or Tier 1 complete. |

## 1. No leakage — new code and UI

Shipped / current tags are those **already in the product catalogs**. Do
not invent a shorter list. See
[`compliance-artifacts-must-localize.mdc`](compliance-artifacts-must-localize.mdc)
and [`enterprise-localization.mdc`](enterprise-localization.mdc).

Typical admin SPA: `en` plus every derived pack already on disk (`en-GB`,
`de`, `fr`, `es`, `zh-Hans`, `zh-TW`, and any later shipped tag). Native
GUIs and product agents: every tag `pim-app-config-i18n` already ships.

| Required | Forbidden |
| --- | --- |
| New SPA / configurator / API chrome keys land in US English source **and every currently shipped content language** in the same change set | English-only new operator UI; “we’ll translate later” for code/UI |
| Missing string → reload once, then named string-ID error + log | Silent English fallback in a loaded non-English pack; raw keys in chrome |
| Product agent GUI/CLI chrome matches the same current-language set | Shipping a new agent string in English only |

Missing-string healer:
[`release-data-self-heal.mdc`](release-data-self-heal.mdc). Lab /
identity / agent-thinking strings in browser-shipped UI:
[`no-lab-config-in-operator-ui.mdc`](no-lab-config-in-operator-ui.mdc)
(cross-ref only — do not duplicate that rule).

## 2. Installers — `en` + `de` only for now

Keep this **distinct** from
[`multilingual-tier-1-installer.mdc`](multilingual-tier-1-installer.mdc):

- That rule still requires **spec packs and product locale catalogs** to
  live in `core-assets` and be harvestable into the install tree.
- **This** rule’s installer exception is **wizard / setup language
  configuration** = `en` + `de` only **for the moment**.
- If product runtime catalogs (SPA `locales/ui`, server `locales`, agent
  `pim-app-config-i18n` packs) already ship extra tags **inside** the MSI
  payload, **do not delete them** to “match” the wizard. Wizard config ≠
  strip runtime packs. Honest report: wizard `en`+`de`; runtime
  agents/UI still all current languages.

## 3. Training guides and manuals — prepared, not translated yet

Narrow, **temporary** exception. Applies to:

- Operator manuals and repo SOPs under `docs/ops/`
- Future in-product Documentation chapters
- MSP / C3PAO demo **training guide** (the CMMC demo guide)

**Prepared for localization** means, in the **same change set**: US
English source **and** a `core-assets/content/localization-work/` queue
row ([`localization-work-queue.mdc`](localization-work-queue.mdc)).

Do **not** require full Tier-1 / all-current-language catalogs for that
body text **for now**. Do **not** close the queue item with agent-draft
translations. Do **not** claim the manual is localized.

**Product chrome around them is still UI** and follows §1: nav labels,
PDF export button, chapter list chrome — all current languages.

**Workforce training / welcome letters** are a **different** surface
([`training-materials-plain-language-and-images.mdc`](training-materials-plain-language-and-images.mdc)).
If those ship in product UI, they follow §1 (full current-language
catalogs), not this manuals exception — unless they are only English repo
drafts queued the same way.

## Forbidden constructs

- New operator UI, API chrome, configurator, or **product agent** string
  in English only
- Silent English fallback or raw i18n keys in a loaded non-English pack
- “We’ll translate later” for new code/UI (manuals exception only)
- Adding installer **wizard** catalogs beyond `en` and `de` in this phase,
  **or** claiming the installer is Tier 1 complete
- Deleting extra runtime locale packs from the MSI so the wizard and
  runtime “match”
- Closing a manuals queue row with agent-draft translations, or claiming
  a manual is localized
- Claiming Met / certified from catalogs existing
  ([`compliance-claims-honesty.mdc`](compliance-claims-honesty.mdc))

## Required agent behavior

1. New SPA / configurator / API / **product agent** strings: US English
   source plus every currently shipped tag in the **same change set**.
2. New installer wizard / setup strings: `en` and `de` only; mark
   installer locale **Partial**; do not claim Tier 1 installer complete.
3. New training guide / operator manual body: English + localization-work
   queue row; do not ship or close full catalogs for that body yet.
   Localize surrounding chrome per §1.
4. Do not strip runtime packs already in the MSI to match the wizard.
5. Mirror this rule to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same change
   set ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)) — the workspace
   `.cursor` directory is not a git root.

## Worked violation → fix

**Violation.** An agent adds a “Retry scan” button on an admin page and a
new AIC Agent tray string, both hardcoded English. The MSI wizard is
extended with French. A new operator manual chapter ships English-only
with no queue row. The report says “Tier 1 installer complete.”

**Fix.** Land `Retry scan` / tray strings in `en` and every current SPA /
`pim-app-config-i18n` tag in the same change set. Leave the installer
language picker at `en`+`de` (Partial). Keep any extra runtime locale
files already in the MSI. Author the manual in US English, add a
localization-work queue row, and do not claim the chapter is localized.
Nav / PDF button labels for that chapter still go into all current UI
packs.

